-- title:
--   Convergence of the finite Euler product
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field with ring of integers $\mathcal O_K$, and write $N(I)=|\mathcal O_K/I|$ for the norm of a nonzero integral ideal. Let $D$ be complex coefficient data on the nonzero integral ideals, normalized by $D(\mathcal O_K)=1$ and multiplicative on relatively prime ideals. Let $S$ be a finite set of nonzero prime ideals and $s\in\mathbb C$. Assume each local series $\sum_{e\ge0}D(P^e)N(P)^{-es}$ for $P\in S$ is absolutely convergent. Let $a_{D,S}(n)$ be the sum of $D(I)$ over the ideals of norm $n$ whose prime factors all belong to $S$.
--
--   $$
--   \sum_{n=1}^{\infty}|a_{D,S}(n)n^{-s}|<\infty.
--   $$
--
--   Absolute convergence of finitely many local factors controls the norm-regrouped series with that finite prime support.
